  "output": {
    "answer": "Beyond the bar and the flag, each run got hard caps set before it started — a cap on tool calls, on wall-clock time, and on spend, written into the lane brief rather than buried in a config file. Production also had guard rails that refuse unsafe configuration at boot, and the gate itself was judged offline against frozen, recorded data rather than a live session, so nothing merges on a live judgment call. Each run also got a named end time instead of an open-ended 'overnight.' It wasn't airtight — before I added a watchdog, an idle tab used up a full day's API allowance overnight.",
